cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic (13.919-Octave, 0.0905-1401.36 um) Space-Lyman to JCMT Millimeter, SOFIA EXES, IRTF SpeX, JWST, Coherent Keplerian Jerk-Drift, Frequency-Comb, Radio & Photometric Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and pure-stdlib numerical audits
  for panchromatic space Lyman-limit/FUV/NUV (FUSE 0.0905-0.1187 um, HST/COS G130M
  0.1125-0.1450 um, HST/STIS E140H R=114,000 FUV, HST/STIS E140M 0.1145-0.1710 um,
  HST/STIS E230M/E230H 0.1605-0.3150 um), ground near-UV (VLT UVES_NUV), optical (HARPS,
  HARPS-N, ESPRESSO HR/UHR, Gemini GHOST BLUE+RED with simultaneous sky-IFU veto, Gemini
  GRACES, Euler CORALIE, OHP SOPHIE, OHP ELODIE, CFHT ESPaDOnS, MPG/ESO FEROS, VLT
  FLAMES/GIRAFFE HR), far-red (VLT UVES_RED, CARMENES_VIS with SERVAL RV alignment), 3-arm
  simultaneous UVB+VIS+NIR (VLT X-shooter 0.2989-2.4790 um), near-infrared NIR/QCL (IRTF
  SpeX 0.80-5.43 um), YJH (NIRPS_HE), thermal J/H/K (VLT CRIRES+), SDSS APOGEE-2 H-band
  (up to N=28 visits), simultaneous YJHK (CFHT SPIRou APERO 0.7.295), JWST space
  optical-to-thermal-IR (NIRISS SOSS, NIRSpec G140H/G235H/G395H, MIRI LRS/MRS),
  continuous ISO SWS (2.36-45.39 um), airborne IR (SOFIA EXES 5.62-26.13 um, R~90,000;
  SOFIA FORCAST 4-grism G063/G111/G227/G329), Spitzer IRS SL+LL (5.20-37.86356 um),
  Herschel far-IR/THz (PACS 51-210 um, SPIRE FTS 194-670.69 um, HIFI 0.56-1.16 THz at
  R=2.2e6), SOFIA GREAT super-THz heterodyne (1.2-4.7 THz, up to R=1.94e7), and JCMT
  submm/mm heterodyne (HARP/RxA3/Uu 213.93-691 GHz, 433.6-1401.36089 um) laser,
  36-campaign exact Keplerian + cubic-jerk coherent shift-stack drift (DRIFT_V57 across
  36 N>=4 campaigns / 56,270 trajectories / 3,566,447,968 pixel integrals / 47,580
  Keplerian polishes), greenhouse CCF, Dyson waste-heat vs. silicate-belt discrimination,
  and periodic frequency-comb technosignatures (0.0905-1401.36089 um, 13.919 unbroken
  octaves across 36 spectrographs / 57 arms; 516 unique stars and 2,797 archival exposures
  totaling 942.7045 h across V3.0-V5.7 + COMB_V4_1 with Keplerian planetary de-Doppler
  across 145 orbital campaigns, 44,124 synthetic calibration trials, 513,887 Legacy V2 false
  alarms eliminated, deterministic Stage-2 physical triage, and uniform all-sky COMB_V4_1
  filtering across 464 stacks), unified with 1.4 GHz Parkes/GBT radio searches and TESS
  photometry achieving 23/23 (100%) radio-echelle closure across a 516-system synthesis
  (0 verified ETI detections; 0.0973 W HST_STIS Proxima Cen, 0.065460 kW HST_STIS_E140H
  Alpha Cen A, 0.039712 kW JWST_NIRISS_SOSS SIMP 0136, 0.455538 kW CARMENES_VIS GJ 1286,
  40.19 kW ESO_UVES GJ 422, 57.04 kW IRTF_SpeX DX Cnc, 33,883.11 kW SOFIA_EXES mu UMa,
  70.703128 kW HERSCHEL_SPIRE_FTS AB Aur, 2,040,500 kW JCMT_HARP LkCa 15, 4,222,791 kW
  JCMT_MM_230GHZ HD 163296, 19,268,981 kW SOFIA_GREAT HD 141569, 21,388,409 kW SOFIA_FORCAST
  HD 166191, 235,044.17 kW HERSCHEL_HIFI R Dor, 71 calibrated panchromatic bridges across
  827 cells [77 multi-phase targets] alongside 175 <10 pc stars with 1.4627 kW median
  limit).
